    a: "The same rules run. No heat below 40°F still dispatches. Cooling calls, tune-ups, and filter questions book a slot or take a message. They do not all page the on-call tech. Surge capacity is the rotation you wrote before the week hit: who is on call, who is backup, and which stretch of I-49 and Highway 71 between Fayetteville and Bentonville they cover. The setup does not add trucks, and it will not tell a caller a truck is on the way when your list says it is not.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can it handle Spanish-speaking callers and bilingual crews?",
    a: "Northwest Arkansas has an English and Spanish caller base, and HVAC crews here are bilingual too. A setup that only works in English is not answering for the calls you actually get. What the build can and cannot do in Spanish, today, is something we demonstrate on the assessment call rather than promise in print. If you want the dispatch to note that the caller was speaking Spanish, that is a question in the script, and the tech you named for those calls is the one who gets the page.",
  },
